Chung, S., Christoudias, C.M., Darrell, T., et al. (2012).    
        <a href="https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1111/acem.12013/abstract?cb=14" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <strong>A Novel Image-based Tool to Reunite Children With Their Families After Disasters.</strong>
        </a>

Academic Emergency Medicine, 19(11): 1227-1234.    
</div>
<div class="document-description">
This article reports the findings of tests completed to determine the accuracy of various child identification tools.  One tool, “Feature-Attribute-Matching,” extracts facial features from photographs to be matched with a parent's description of their child. The other tool, "User-Feedback," allows parents to choose photographs resembling their child which then reprioritizes the images in the database.</div>

