Corfield, J. and Tanner Health. (2026).    
        <a href="https://www.centralfladisaster.org/_files/ugd/8d7960_b6430a969abf48e4ab3fe3e72a186784.pdf?cb=13805" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <strong>Family and Loved Ones Reunification Process.</strong>
        </a>

    
</div>
<div class="document-description">
Emergency managers can use this paper-based toolkit to reduce the time it takes to match loved ones with a patient. It includes blank and many pre-scripted sets of (fictional patient) forms, including triage tags, a loved one/next of kin form, a mass casualty patient tracking card , and a reunification information form. The completed sets illustrate the wide range of injuries and situations patients will present during a mass casualty incident.</div>

