National Center for Missing and Exploited Children (NCMEC) (n.d.).    
        <a href="https://umr.missingkids.org/umr/reportUMR?execution=e1s1&amp;cb=468" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
            <strong>Unaccompanied Minors Registry.</strong>
        </a>

(Accessed 11/23/2022.)     
</div>
<div class="document-description">
This data collection tool is focused on collecting basic information of children who have been separated from their families as a result of a disaster. Individuals can provide basic information and photos concerning a located child whose parents are missing. Once registration information is submitted, NCMEC will cross-reference it against any potential phone calls from a child’s parents who may be searching for their child.</div>

